module gunbc.native_cli_door_probe

// THE V2-NATIVE CLI'S POSITIVE CONTROL, AND THE REASON IT IS ITS OWN SOURCE ROOT.
//
// `//gunbc/instruments:v2-native-cli` emits and BUILDS `v2.cli.compile_cli`; until the step that
// consumes this file landed, that was the whole instrument -- the door compiled and was never
// walked through, which DESIGN section 5 names as specification-without-execution: a green that
// establishes the closure typechecks and nothing about whether the program runs. This file is the
// argv the built binary is handed so that it does run: `emit --entry
// gunbc.native_cli_door_probe --source-root fixtures/native_cli_door/dag`.
//
// IT HAS NO IMPORTS, for the same reason `fixture.closure.rustc_green_probe` has none: the
// entry resolves against the roots the argv bound, so a module whose
// closure is itself is the SMALLEST subject that still walks argv parse, source-root binding, acquisition,
// resolution and emission end to end. A subject with imports would add nothing to what the door
// decides and would make a red attributable to the import graph rather than to the door.
//
// IT IS ITS OWN DIRECTORY AND NOT A FILE IN AN EXISTING FIXTURE ROOT, and it sits at the position its
// name derives under `gunbc.source_layout` (`gunbc/native_cli_door_probe.dag` under the tree
// directory the argv names). The name is in a declared namespace (`gunbc.source_layout_namespaces`)
// because the census control enumerates the root's population from the declared rows: a module in a
// namespace no row declares would be a population the census cannot see. The CLI reads the file its
// entry NAME derives and the files that file's own text requests, and nothing else, so no neighbour
// can change the control's closure; a separate directory still keeps the control's subject one file
// a reader can see whole.
// The argument is the dag tree's directory (`.../dag`), which the CLI recognises as the dag tree.
//
// THE DECLARATION'S NAME AND VALUE ARE WHAT THE CONTROL READS. v2 lowers this `data` declaration to
// a named member whose body is the literal, and the door renders it through the Rust target's
// declared rows as `fn native_cli_door_probe_value() -> i32 { 606060 }`. The emit arm admits an exit 0
// only when the text names `native_cli_door_probe_value`, carries `606060` AND is Rust the build's
// compiler accepts; the body refusal it pinned from gunbc#12207 until then is now its regression.
//
// The declaration is deliberately trivial: one literal of a kernel type, with no imports.
data native_cli_door_probe_value: Int = 606060
